					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12863230#post-4450725</guid>
				<title>Author Post</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12863230/scp-4943#post-4450725</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 20 Dec 2019 18:09:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Attila the Pun</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1685633</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>While Brain Uploading (as tvtropes calls it) isn't an uncommon trope, most of the stories about it seem to focus on the philosophical questions that come with it. I haven't seen much that covers what it would actually be like for the AI, aside from handwaving it with a physics simulation or the like. What would it look like when you take a copy of someone and then drop it into a computer?</p> <p>This is a story about that.</p> <p>Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malycegraves" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4916887&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606801228" alt="MalyceGraves" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4916887)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malycegraves" >MalyceGraves</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/voct" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=392303&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606801228" alt="Voct" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=392303)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/voct" >Voct</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5255688&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606801228" alt="DrAkimoto" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5255688)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" >DrAkimoto</a></span>, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-fullham" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1989312&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606801228" alt="Doctor Fullham" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1989312)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-fullham" >Doctor Fullham</a></span> for crit!</p> <p>Also, credit goes to these people who <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">were crazy enough to</span> let me use their characters:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/osiris-wentworth-and-his-wonderful-day-at-work">Osiris Wentworth</a> created by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/moreworldliness" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5006778&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606801228" alt="MoreWorldliness" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5006778)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/moreworldliness" >MoreWorldliness</a></span></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/why-clef-hates-cupcakes">Quinn E. Roscoe</a> created by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/detectiveroscoe" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5068157&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606801228" alt="detectiveroscoe" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5068157)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/detectiveroscoe" >detectiveroscoe</a></span></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/calibri-bold-s-mega-cool-office">Dr. C. Bold</a> created by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5045819&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606801228" alt="Calibri Bold" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5045819)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold" >Calibri Bold</a></span></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/michael-sends-his-regards">Dr. Nathaniel Bishop</a> created by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themanhattenproject" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3809943&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606801228" alt="TheManhattenProject" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3809943)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themanhattenproject" >TheManhattenProject</a></span></li> </ul> <p><strong>EDIT 2020/11/30:</strong> I went with the current version of the text logs as a stylistic choice, but I realized later that it might be nice for translators or whoever to know who is talking. So I'm working on a color-coded version of this. Expect that within the next few weeks, but for now, here's some details about each character's speech patterns. In order of introduction:</p> <ul> <li><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Dr. Bold</strong></span> is the most obvious: he &quot;speaks&quot; in all caps.</li> <li><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Morgan Fish</strong></span> is the most &quot;normal.&quot; His capitalization is correct, and he uses some punctuation, but not all of it. For example, his speech uses periods and commas but drops apostrophes.</li> <li><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Osiris Wentworth</strong></span> speaks in all lowercase and doesn't use any punctuation at all. He puts each sentence on a new line.</li> <li><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Quinn Roscoe</strong></span> uses correct punctuation, but speaks entirely in lowercase.</li> <li><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Dr. Nathaniel Bishop</strong></span> is &quot;glitchy&quot;. I literally just opened a hex editor and flipped random bits of his lines. He shares this with the unnamed dead guy in the first log, and Morgan also develops quirk this later on as he gets overstressed and &quot;destabilizes&quot;.</li> </ul> <p>God help you if you try to translate this into a logographic language.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
